{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"d2b69be861e0399ca189d66cc4119a5fab774b8fdcb5e98e45ada3ee0e73191d","digest":{"component_or_area":"grounding worker harness","key_entities":["src/rebar/grounding/harness.py","src/rebar/grounding/__init__.py","run_in_worker","multiprocessing.get_context","Process.start","RunResult","SpawnProcess","ForkProcess","docs/env-vars.md","tests/unit/grounding/test_spawn_contract.py"],"problem_keywords":["multiprocessing","fork","spawn","deadlock","pickling","serialization","CPython 3.12","deprecation warning","thread safety"],"propositions":["The grounding worker harness hard-codes POSIX fork via multiprocessing.get_context('fork'), which triggers CPython 3.12 DeprecationWarning when called from multithreaded hosts and will become unsafe in CPython 3.14.","The fork-based harness accepts unpickleable callables (closures, lambdas) that fail under spawn, requiring an explicit callable/serialization contract before switching defaults.","Process construction, start, and serialization failures plus parent receive/unpickling failures must map to fail-open RunResult(abstain_reason='other') rather than propagate.","Switching default context to spawn preserves 46/47 existing lifecycle tests; the one failure is a fixture with an unpickleable local closure that must be replaced with a parent-only proxy."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787879003772610001,"uuid":"f6a8e104-6ef0-42e0-97e1-adc5adeb48f6"}